\description{
\code{\link[=uploadCollectionToZenodo]{uploadCollectionToZenodo()}} creates a \strong{collection record} on
\href{https://zenodo.org}{Zenodo} as a \strong{draft}: a record with its own DOI that
groups published Zenodo records, so that they can be cited together. There
are two levels of collections:
\itemize{
\item an \strong{owner collection} groups the MR1 data packages (campaigns) of one
owner, e.g. all campaigns of the Swiss Ornithological Institute;
\item the \strong{community collection} groups the owner collections of the BirdScan
MR1 community.
}

The collection is described in a YAML file, see
\code{\link[=createCollectionMetadataTemplate]{createCollectionMetadataTemplate()}}. The collection record:
\itemize{
\item links to each member with a \code{HasPart} related identifier. The links point
to the concept DOI of the member, so they stay valid when a member gets a
new version;
\item holds the file \code{members.csv}, with per member the concept DOI, the DOI,
record ID, title, version and publication date of its latest version, its
period and its Zenodo link, at the time of the upload;
\item gets the period (\code{Collected}) of its members.
}

With \code{linkMembers = TRUE} (default), an \code{IsPartOf} link to the concept DOI
of the collection is added to each member, with
\code{\link[=addZenodoRelatedIdentifiers]{addZenodoRelatedIdentifiers()}}. These edits of the members are \strong{not
published}, because the collection itself is a draft: first check and
publish the collection on Zenodo, then publish the edits of the members with
\code{\link[=linkCollectionMembers]{linkCollectionMembers()}} and \code{publish = TRUE} (or on Zenodo). Links can
only be added to records of your own Zenodo account; members that cannot be
linked are reported in a warning.

\strong{New versions.} To add or remove members, add them to the \code{members} of the
metadata file, increase \code{version}, and set \code{id} to the DOI of the published
collection. The upload then creates a new version of the collection record.
The \code{HasPart} links follow the new list of members; other related
identifiers of the previous version are kept.
